## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | IMPORTANT | lib/src/cli/agent_cli_viewer.dart | ⚠️ important deny on error doesn t hold on the tui reset path — the repl keeps driving the new session unleased after a refused claim claimsessionlease now throws stateerror on leaserefused this hunk — but reset calls it after the new session was already created and assigned agent cli commands dart 548 560 dart session await createsession new session s2 assigned await releasesessionlease await claimsessionlease ← stateerror thrown here on refuse in tui mode the throw lands in runcontainedsubmit agent cli composer dart 36 45 which by contract never rethrows … the session stays usable — so the refusal renders as a one line error panel and the repl continues with session the brand new session heldleasepath null viewer null the next user message goes through sendusermessage → startrun and drives s2 with no lease and no re claim claimsessionlease runs only at boot and reset that is the exact hole this pr closes if the store failure is transient nfs hiccup disk pressure and another process later opens s2 it sees no sidecar acquires and you have two writers — the second writer scenario hole 2 hole 3 just eliminated elsewhere suggested shape after a refused claim in reset restore the previous session binding or clear session flip the cli into the same refused and idle state the boot path produces so a refused claim can never be followed by an unleased drive a regression test asserting post refusal submit does not run a turn would pin it interactive boot is unaffected the throw there escapes run before the repl accepts input — loud denial contract holds |
| F2 | open | IMPORTANT | lib/src/cli/agent_cli_viewer.dart | ⚠️ important headless refusal does not exit through the runheadless catch — it escapes to the crash handler and neither cli arm has a test two related problems on this new leaserefused arm 1 the throw bypasses runheadless s error handling claimsessionleaseheadless is called at agent cli dart 2361 which is before the first try inside runheadless agent cli dart 2444 the stateerror therefore escapes runheadless entirely — its catch error … return 1 is never reached the only caller is bin fah runapp dart 2210 2221 whose try finally around await headlessrun has no catch either so the error surfaces via the zoned uncaught handler bin fah dart 113 125 → handleuncaughterror bin fah util dart 214 stderr prints fa crashed stateerror lease cannot prove this session is free publishfailed — refusing to drive and appends a full stack trace to fah crash log before exit 1 the safety property holds refuse non zero exit never drive but a controlled refusal is now indistinguishable from a real crash in the crash triage channel cron wake loops hitting a persistent store outage will fill crash log with non crash stack traces and the pr description s claim headless exits 1 through the runheadless catch does not match the shipped mechanism route the refusal through runheadless s guarded section or return a dedicated refusal exit code like the blocked path s 3 so it prints the clean error line and skips the crash log write 2 no test coverage for either new cli branch the pr s 27 core tests cover the store and the app manager but neither the interactive tuierror abort arm nor the headless throw arm in agent cli viewer dart is exercised by any test grep leaserefused test cli is empty the only existing cli lease tests still pass because they never hit the refused branch please add a refused claim in headless mode exits non zero without driving a turn and the interactive arm prints the refusal and does not start a run |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

